-- title:
--   Analytic regularity of the Bianchi IX constraint
-- statement:
--   For real variables $p,s,a,b,c$, set
--   $$K=a^2+b^2+c^2-2(ab+bc+ca),\qquad S=p^2+s^2,\qquad C=S+K.$$
--   The shear components and wall rates are
--   $$P=Kp-2a^2+b^2+c^2+ab-2bc+ac,$$
--   $$Q=Ks+\sqrt{3}(-b^2+c^2+ab-ac),$$
--   $$r_1=-S+2p,\qquad r_2=-S-p+\sqrt{3}s,\qquad r_3=-S-p-\sqrt{3}s.$$
--   These functions define the normalized vacuum Bianchi IX vector field
--   $(P,Q,r_1a,r_2b,r_3c)$.
--
--   Let $X=\mathbb R^5$ with coordinates $x=(p,s,a,b,c)$ and the sup norm. Write
--   $$F(x)=(P,Q,r_1a,r_2b,r_3c),\qquad \mathcal C(x)=C(p,s,a,b,c),$$
--   and let $W=\{(p,s,a,b,c)\in X:a>0,\ b>0,\ c>0\}$.
--
--   The constraint function $\mathcal C:X\to\mathbb R$ is $C^n$ for every
--   $n\in\mathbb N\cup\{\infty,\omega\}$, including the analytic order $\omega$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/l46430640-del/ERA-STATISTICS-FORMAL/blob/d74c241819f896ab8d050b21ace80c8e90eabd9e/BianchiIX/Dynamics/Normalized.lean#L36-L38

